 "summary": "On an ETOPS flight, four technical criteria govern a re-routing or diversion: loss of NAT-HLA capability, diversion airports going below minima or becoming unsuitable, LAND ASAP failures, and failures whose increased fuel consumption exceeds the reserves. After an engine or IDG failure, start the APU and use its electrical channel. After an engine failure, the fixed speed strategy is the one recommended for ETOPS: M.78/320 kt at MCT, the approved one-engine-inoperative diversion speed.",
