  {
   "title": "ETOPS abnormal and emergency procedures",
   "source": "FCOM PRO-SPO-40-50 (HS-TX)",
   "lines": [
    {
     "kind": "condition",
     "text": "ELECTRICAL EMERGENCY CONFIGURATION. Complete the ECAM procedure using the following:",
     "level": 0,
     "applies_to": [
      "all"
     ],
     "refs": [
      {
       "book": "FCOM",
       "code": "PRO-SPO-40-50",
       "page": "P 1/4",
       "pdf": 4588
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "info",
     "text": "AIR CONDITIONING: As cockpit and cabin temperature control is lost, it is recommended to open the cockpit door.",
     "level": 1,
     "applies_to": [
      "all"
     ],
     "refs": [
      {
       "book": "FCOM",
       "code": "PRO-SPO-40-50",
       "page": "P 1/4",
       "pdf": 4588
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "info",
     "text": "FUEL: As all fuel pumps are lost, the engines are fed by gravity. Refer to GRVTY FUEL FEEDING Procedure.",
     "level": 1,
     "applies_to": [
      "all"
     ],
     "refs": [
      {
       "book": "FCOM",
       "code": "PRO-SPO-40-50",
       "page": "P 1/4",
       "pdf": 4588
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "info",
     "text": "ENGINE ANTI-ICE: Engine anti-ice valves are permanently open, although the ECAM memo ENG A. ICE is not displayed on the ECAM (except if the ENG A. ICE pb is at ON).",
     "level": 1,
     "applies_to": [
      "all"
     ],
     "refs": [
      {
       "book": "FCOM",
       "code": "PRO-SPO-40-50",
       "page": "P 2/4",
       "pdf": 4589
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "info",
     "text": "WING ANTI-ICE: If only one ENG BLEED is available, PACK 1 must be switched OFF, to avoid having both packs and wing anti-ice supplied by a single bleed source.",
     "level": 1,
     "applies_to": [
      "all"
     ],
     "refs": [
      {
       "book": "FCOM",
       "code": "PRO-SPO-40-50",
       "page": "P 2/4",
       "pdf": 4589
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "info",
     "text": "ENGINE: As the engines are in degraded N1 mode, the power setting has to be done using tables.",
     "level": 1,
     "applies_to": [
      "all"
     ],
     "refs": [
      {
       "book": "FCOM",
       "code": "PRO-SPO-40-50",
       "page": "P 2/4",
       "pdf": 4589
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "info",
     "text": "BLUE HYDRAULIC CIRCUIT LOW LEVEL OR LOW PRESSURE OR OVERHEAT: Start the APU to ensure availability of the APU generator.",
     "level": 0,
     "applies_to": [
      "all"
     ],
     "refs": [
      {
       "book": "FCOM",
       "code": "PRO-SPO-40-50",
       "page": "P 2/4",
       "pdf": 4589
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "info",
     "text": "ENGINE OR IDG FAILURE: Start the APU and use the APU electrical channel.",
     "level": 0,
     "applies_to": [
      "all"
     ],
     "refs": [
      {
       "book": "FCOM",
       "code": "PRO-SPO-40-50",
       "page": "P 2/4",
       "pdf": 4589
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "info",
     "text": "LOSS OF AIR CONDITIONING: In the case of loss of the air conditioning capability (loss of both packs, loss of both bleeds without APU bleed etc.), when at FL 100 with the RAM AIR opened, the CAB FANS must be switched off.",
     "level": 0,
     "applies_to": [
      "all"
     ],
     "refs": [
      {
       "book": "FCOM",
       "code": "PRO-SPO-40-50",
       "page": "P 2/4",
       "pdf": 4589
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "status": null,
 "background": [
  {
   "text": "When an engine failure occurs during cruise, three strategies apply: standard, obstacle and fixed speed. Unless a specific procedure has been established before dispatch (considering ETOPS or mountainous areas), the standard strategy is used.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-ENG",
